{"timestamp":1774890581148,"source_app":"agentic-harness","session_id":"a9cce13f-e047-4c4a-ac87-3480b05083b4","hook_event_type":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01VRGSfQg4BFWv2c6G6DPXGq","payload":{"session_id":"a9cce13f-e047-4c4a-ac87-3480b05083b4","transcript_path":"/Users/rivero/.claude/projects/-Users-rivero-ai-agentic-experience-apps-mas-trees-ddae437f/a9cce13f-e047-4c4a-ac87-3480b05083b4.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/ddae437f","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/ddae437f/.pinata/specs/issue-11-adw-ddae437f-sdlc_planner-prevent-duplicate-fragment-title-clone.md","content":"# Plan: Prevent duplicate Fragment Title for cloned cards in M@S Studio\n\n## Summary\nWhen a card is cloned in M@S Studio, the clone dialog pre-fills the title field with the original title, which can result in two fragments sharing the same Fragment Title under the same tag path. This plan adds a uniqueness check scoped to the parent path: before the clone dialog opens, a unique title suggestion is computed by scanning existing fragments and incrementing a numeric suffix (`-1`, `-2`, \u2026) until a free slot is found. The dialog pre-fills this suggestion; users may still edit it freely. The same deduplication is also applied inside `copyFragment()` in the repository as a safety net.\n\n## Task Description\nIntroduce a `generateUniqueTitle(baseTitle, parentPath)` method on `MasRepository` that:\n- Searches all fragments under `parentPath` using the existing AEM search API\n- Collects their titles\n- Parses the `baseTitle` to strip any trailing `-N` numeric suffix and determine the canonical base\n- Increments a counter suffix (`-1`, `-2`, \u2026) until a title is found that does not exist in the result set\n- Returns the unique title string\n\nWire this into:\n1. `showClone()` in `mas-fragment-editor.js` \u2014 pre-populate `this.titleClone` before opening the dialog, and update the dialog `value` binding to reflect `this.titleClone`\n2. `showClone()` in `editor-panel.js` \u2014 same change for the parallel editor panel component\n3. `copyFragment()` in `mas-repository.js` \u2014 if `updatedTitle` is empty/falsy, call `generateUniqueTitle` and always save with a unique title (safety net in case the dialog is bypassed)\n\n## Relevant Files\n\n| File | Action | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| `studio/src/mas-repository.js` | Edit | Add `generateUniqueTitle()` method; update `copyFragment()` to use it as a fallback |\n| `studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js` | Edit | Pre-populate `titleClone` in `showClone()`; update clone dialog `value` binding |\n| `studio/src/editor-panel.js` | Edit | Same as above for the parallel editor panel |\n| `studio/test/mas-repository.test.js` | Edit | Add unit tests for `generateUniqueTitle()` |\n\n## Step by Step Tasks\n\n### 1. Add `generateUniqueTitle` to `mas-repository.js`\n\nAdd the following method to `MasRepository`:\n\n```js\n/**\n * Finds a unique fragment title scoped to a parent path.\n * Strips any existing trailing -N suffix from baseTitle, then increments\n * until a title is not taken by any fragment in parentPath.\n * @param {string} baseTitle - The original fragment title\n * @param {string} parentPath - The parent folder path to scope uniqueness\n * @returns {Promise<string>} A title that does not conflict with existing fragments\n */\nasync generateUniqueTitle(baseTitle, parentPath) {\n    // Strip existing trailing numeric suffix: \"foo-2\" -> \"foo\", \"foo-bar-3\" -> \"foo-bar\"\n    const suffixMatch = baseTitle.match(/^(.*)-(\\d+)$/);\n    const canonical = suffixMatch ? suffixMatch[1] : baseTitle;\n\n    // Collect titles of all fragments in the parent path\n    const existingTitles = new Set();\n    try {\n        const generator = this.aem.sites.cf.fragments.search({ path: parentPath });\n        for await (const items of generator) {\n            for (const item of items ?? []) {\n                if (item?.title) existingTitles.add(item.title);\n            }\n        }\n    } catch {\n        // If search fails, return a best-effort suffix-1 title\n        return `${canonical}-1`;\n    }\n\n    // Return canonical if not taken, otherwise increment\n    if (!existingTitles.has(canonical)) return canonical;\n    let counter = 1;\n    while (existingTitles.has(`${canonical}-${counter}`)) {\n        counter++;\n    }\n    return `${canonical}-${counter}`;\n}\n```\n\nPlace this method alongside `copyFragment` in the same class.\n\n### 2. Update `copyFragment` in `mas-repository.js` as a safety net\n\nAfter obtaining `result` from `this.aem.sites.cf.fragments.copy(this.fragmentInEdit)`, always resolve a unique title before deciding to save:\n\n- Compute `parentPath = this.fragmentInEdit.path.split('/').slice(0, -1).join('/')`\n- If `updatedTitle` is falsy, resolve via `generateUniqueTitle(this.fragmentInEdit.title, parentPath)`\n- If `updatedTitle` is provided, use it as-is (the user typed it in the dialog)\n- Set `needsSave = resolvedTitle !== result.title || osi` (always save if the title differs from what AEM produced)\n- Update `result.title = resolvedTitle` before saving\n\nThis ensures no duplicate title even if `confirmClone` is called programmatically without a `titleClone`.\n\n### 3. Pre-populate `titleClone` in `showClone()` \u2014 `mas-fragment-editor.js`\n\nIn `showClone()` (around line 1088), before setting `showCloneDialog = true`:\n\n```js\nasync showClone() {\n    if (Store.editor.hasChanges) {\n        const confirmed = await this.promptDiscardChanges();\n        if (!confirmed) return;\n    }\n    const parentPath = this.fragment.path.split('/').slice(0, -1).join('/');\n    this.titleClone = await this.repository.generateUniqueTitle(this.fragment.title, parentPath);\n    this.showCloneDialog = true;\n    Store.showCloneDialog.set(true);\n}\n```\n\n### 4. Update clone dialog `value` binding \u2014 `mas-fragment-editor.js`\n\nIn `get cloneConfirmationDialog` (around line 1232), the textfield currently has:\n\n```html\nvalue=\"${this.fragment.title}\"\n```\n\nChange it to:\n\n```html\nvalue=\"${this.titleClone}\"\n```\n\nThis ensures the dialog input reflects the pre-computed unique title.\n\n### 5. Pre-populate `titleClone` in `showClone()` \u2014 `editor-panel.js`\n\nSame change as Step 3 applied to `showClone()` in `editor-panel.js` (around line 620):\n\n```js\nasync showClone() {\n    if (Store.editor.hasChanges) {\n        const confirmed = await this.promptDiscardChanges();\n        if (!confirmed) return;\n    }\n    const parentPath = this.fragment.path.split('/').slice(0, -1).join('/');\n    this.titleClone = await this.repository.generateUniqueTitle(this.fragment.title, parentPath);\n    this.showCloneDialog = true;\n    Store.showCloneDialog.set(true);\n}\n```\n\n### 6. Update clone dialog `value` binding \u2014 `editor-panel.js`\n\nIn `get cloneConfirmationDialog` in `editor-panel.js` (around line 881), the textfield currently has:\n\n```html\nvalue=\"${this.fragment.title}\"\n```\n\nChange it to:\n\n```html\nvalue=\"${this.titleClone}\"\n```\n\n### 7. Add unit tests for `generateUniqueTitle` \u2014 `mas-repository.test.js`\n\nAdd a `describe('generateUniqueTitle', ...)` block that covers:\n\n- Returns the canonical base title when it does not exist in the parent path\n- Returns `canonical-1` when the canonical title already exists\n- Returns `canonical-2` when both canonical and `canonical-1` already exist\n- Strips an existing `-N` suffix from the input title before computing the base\n- Returns `canonical-1` if the search API throws\n\nUse the existing `createAemMock` and `createRepository` helpers; extend the AEM mock's `search` stub to return an async generator.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Cloning a card whose Fragment Title already exists in the parent path opens the dialog pre-filled with `<original>-1` (or the next available suffix)\n- [ ] Cloning `lucy-card-1` when `lucy-card-1` and `lucy-card` both exist produces `lucy-card-2` (canonical is `lucy-card`, next free is `lucy-card-2`)\n- [ ] Cloning a card whose title does not collide opens the dialog pre-filled with the original title unchanged\n- [ ] The original card's Fragment Title is not modified\n- [ ] Manually editing the pre-filled title in the clone dialog works without restriction\n- [ ] After clone, no two cards under the same path share the same Fragment Title\n- [ ] `generateUniqueTitle` unit tests pass: no-collision, single-collision, multiple-collision, strip-suffix, search-error fallback\n\n## Validation Commands\n\n```\nnode --check studio/src/mas-repository.js\nnode --check studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js\nnode --check studio/src/editor-panel.js\nnode --check studio/test/mas-repository.test.js\n```\n"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VRGSfQg4BFWv2c6G6DPXGq"}}
